    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d866-a1">

                <pb facs="0849" n="535" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg535"/>


                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Van Dyke</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Ambassador
                        in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">The Hague</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 4, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The American Legation at The Hague requests information in regard to regulations
                    and authorization under which the British officials are opening mail of the
                    American Consular Service, some of which, as is evident from the enclosed
                        envelopes,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d866-f1"/> is under official seal.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
